# Build UI only with web-ui (Bloom) components

This app's web-ui components are the `Design*` components in `src/components/ds/` (e.g.
`DesignButton`, `DesignInputSelect`, `DesignDialog`, `DesignDataTable`, `DesignCard`,
`DesignBadge`, `DesignTooltip`, `DesignSideSheet`). Every new or changed feature uses them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: raw HTML, shadcn primitives or one-off styling in feature code
<button className="rounded bg-teal-700 px-3 py-1 text-white">Save</button>
<select>…</select>
import { Dialog } from "@/components/ui/dialog";
<table className="w-full text-sm">…</table>

// ✅ GOOD
<DesignButton variant="filled" theme="primary">Save</DesignButton>
<DesignInputSelect options={options} value={v} onChange={setV} />
<DesignDialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} title="…">…</DesignDialog>
<DesignDataTable columns={columns} data={rows} rowKey={(r) => r.id} />
```

- Custom tables (e.g. editable grids) use `tableStyles` from `src/components/ds/tableStyles.ts`.
- `src/components/ui/*` (shadcn/Radix) is only for building `Design*` components, not for features.
- Use props the component documents; don't restyle it with `className` colours, radii or spacing.
- Colours, spacing and type come from the CSS variables in `src/index.css`, not hex values.

## When something is missing or unclear

The source of truth is the original web-ui repo:
`~/Documents/design-systems/web-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/<Component>`
(`.tsx`, `.scss`/`.css`, `.mdx` guidelines, `.stories.tsx`). The web-ui Storybook MCP
(`user-web-ui-storybook`) has the same docs.

1. Check whether a `Design*` component already covers it.
2. If not, read the web-ui source for that component and add or extend a `Design*`
   component in `src/components/ds/` that matches it (tokens, sizes, states, props), then use it.
3. Never invent props or variants web-ui doesn't have. If web-ui has no such component, say so
   and compose existing `Design*` components instead of hand-styling.
